WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.040 --> 00:00:02.760
A strategy card says one of three things.

2
00:00:02.760 --> 00:00:05.680
In cash, the strategy holds nothing.

3
00:00:05.680 --> 00:00:07.600
Long, it holds the asset,

4
00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:09.520
like TSLA here.

5
00:00:09.520 --> 00:00:12.280
Or short, on the long and short strategies,

6
00:00:12.280 --> 00:00:15.440
like SUI here, a bet on a fall.

7
00:00:15.440 --> 00:00:17.280
That is the whole signal.

8
00:00:17.280 --> 00:00:19.560
Everything else on the card explains it.

9
00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:21.460
When does it change? Each card

10
00:00:21.460 --> 00:00:23.000
says it under its name.

11
00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:24.260
One decision a day,

12
00:00:24.260 --> 00:00:25.690
at the daily close,

13
00:00:25.690 --> 00:00:27.120
midnight UTC.

14
00:00:27.120 --> 00:00:29.410
12-hour strategies decide twice a day,

15
00:00:29.410 --> 00:00:31.920
at midnight, and at noon UTC.

16
00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:35.140
Stock strategies decide after the New York close.

17
00:00:35.140 --> 00:00:37.840
The signal is valid until the next close.

18
00:00:37.840 --> 00:00:39.620
A signal is a decision,

19
00:00:39.620 --> 00:00:41.260
not an execution.

20
00:00:41.260 --> 00:00:43.950
Last change, from Bitcoin to cash,

21
00:00:43.950 --> 00:00:47.760
13 days ago, sold at $81,850.

22
00:00:47.760 --> 00:00:49.100
That is the closing price of

23
00:00:49.100 --> 00:00:51.000
the candle that made the decision,

24
00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:52.160
in the backtest.

25
00:00:52.160 --> 00:00:54.140
Nobody placed an order for you.

26
00:00:54.140 --> 00:00:56.360
What you get is the rules decision.

27
00:00:56.360 --> 00:00:58.520
What you do with it is yours.

28
00:00:58.520 --> 00:01:01.240
So what can you do with it? Three ways.

29
00:01:01.240 --> 00:01:04.600
By hand, on your own exchange after the close.

30
00:01:04.600 --> 00:01:06.860
Automated, with Signum, which can read the

31
00:01:06.860 --> 00:01:08.980
signal and place the order for you.

32
00:01:08.980 --> 00:01:10.680
Or through your AI assistant,

33
00:01:10.680 --> 00:01:12.710
such as Claude, which can read the same

34
00:01:12.710 --> 00:01:15.760
signals through MCP and tell you what changed.

35
00:01:15.760 --> 00:01:18.520
Whichever you choose, the card is the source,

36
00:01:18.520 --> 00:01:20.980
and it is the same card for everyone.

37
00:01:20.980 --> 00:01:22.560
When the signal is not fresh,

38
00:01:22.560 --> 00:01:23.840
the card tells you.

39
00:01:23.840 --> 00:01:26.000
After each close, there is a short window

40
00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:27.840
while the new run is being published.

41
00:01:27.840 --> 00:01:29.210
The card turns amber,

42
00:01:29.210 --> 00:01:32.150
refreshing signal, for up to 45 minutes,

43
00:01:32.150 --> 00:01:34.660
and reloads itself when the new signal is out.

44
00:01:34.660 --> 00:01:35.820
If a run is late,

45
00:01:35.820 --> 00:01:38.420
it turns red, signal expired.

46
00:01:38.420 --> 00:01:40.440
A red card is not a signal.

47
00:01:40.440 --> 00:01:42.120
Wait for it to refresh.

48
00:01:42.120 --> 00:01:44.680
A few things to read without fooling yourself.

49
00:01:44.680 --> 00:01:47.740
Every section has an info icon in plain English.

50
00:01:47.740 --> 00:01:50.480
The card opens on the window since 2023,

51
00:01:50.480 --> 00:01:52.570
and the harder stretch since 2018

52
00:01:52.570 --> 00:01:54.200
is always right below it.

53
00:01:54.200 --> 00:01:55.340
Read both.

54
00:01:55.340 --> 00:01:57.760
The drawdown on the card is measured monthly.

55
00:01:57.760 --> 00:01:59.960
The engine's daily drawdown is worse,

56
00:01:59.960 --> 00:02:01.400
and the Summary shows it.

57
00:02:01.400 --> 00:02:04.340
And long and short strategies are in early access.

58
00:02:04.340 --> 00:02:06.240
Their results are preliminary.

59
00:02:06.240 --> 00:02:07.640
The card decides.

60
00:02:07.640 --> 00:02:09.120
You execute.

61
00:02:09.120 --> 00:02:11.400
Everything here is a simulated backtest,

62
00:02:11.400 --> 00:02:15.110
not real performance, and not investment advice.

